# luminos-drkonqi.slice — a shared memory budget for ALL DrKonqi backtrace jobs.
# [CHANGE: claude-code | 2026-08-29] BUG-084
#
# WHY A SLICE AND NOT `MemoryMax=` ON THE UNIT
# --------------------------------------------
# The obvious fix is a per-instance cap on drkonqi-coredump-launcher@.service. That does not
# actually fix what was measured on 2026-07-24. The incident was not one greedy gdb, it was
# FIVE launchers active at once (Filelight, plus repeated kscreen-doctor and qml crashes,
# each of which arms another instance). A 2G per-instance cap would have permitted 10G on a
# 14 GiB box — a stall, not a fix. drkonqi-coredump-launcher@ is a TEMPLATE, so the number of
# instances is set by how many things crashed, which is exactly the quantity we cannot bound.
#
# A slice caps the SUM. Five concurrent backtraces now share 2G and OOM-kill each other
# inside this cgroup instead of taking the desktop with them.
#
# WHY THESE NUMBERS — AND WHY THERE IS NO MemoryHigh=
# ---------------------------------------------------
# Measured peak on 2026-07-24: gdb at 7.4 GiB RSS / 16.3 GiB VSZ, still climbing after 12
# minutes, with zram 100% full and /proc/pressure/memory full avg10 at 7.85%. So the cap has
# to be far below 7.4G to do anything at all.
#
# The first version of this file paired MemoryMax=2G with MemoryHigh=1500M, on the usual
# reasoning that a soft throttle is gentler than a kill. It was then tested against a process
# that faults in 3 GiB of real anonymous pages, all four combinations, 2026-08-29:
#
#	MemoryHigh  MemorySwapMax  outcome
#	1500M       (allowed)      BREACHED — allocated the full 3 GiB in 10 s
#	off         (allowed)      BREACHED — allocated the full 3 GiB in 7 s
#	1500M       0              LIVELOCK — throttled below 1.6 GiB, still running at 45 s,
#	                                      never killed, never finished
#	off         0              OOM-KILLED at 2 GiB in 2 s   <-- the only one that works
#
# So the shipped-first config was the WORST of the four: with swap available, MemoryHigh does
# not stop a runaway, it just pushes the pages into zram — which is precisely the 2026-07-24
# incident, reproduced. And with swap denied, MemoryHigh prevents the kill from ever
# happening: anonymous pages cannot be reclaimed, so the cgroup spins in direct reclaim making
# near-zero progress and the job neither dies nor completes. A backtrace hung forever is not
# better than one that failed.
#
#   MemoryMax=2G     — hard kill, and the ONLY thing doing any work here. Above this the
#                      backtrace is not going to finish usefully anyway.
#   MemorySwapMax=0  — load-bearing, not a nicety. The specific harm on 2026-07-24 was 8 GiB
#                      of zram filling and every other process stalling on swap-in. Without
#                      this line MemoryMax is unenforceable in practice, because the cgroup
#                      just swaps rather than hitting the limit.
#   MemoryHigh       — deliberately ABSENT. See the table.
#
# WHAT THIS COSTS
# ---------------
# A crash report for a very large core may now be truncated or fail outright. That is the
# intended trade: the core file itself is untouched in ~/.cache/drkonqi/cores/ and in
# coredumpctl, so a backtrace can always be produced by hand afterwards with
# `coredumpctl gdb <pid>`. Nothing is lost that was not already on disk.
#
# This is INSURANCE, not the root fix. The root fix is that kscreen-doctor reliably SIGABRTs
# on this box and keeps arming new launchers; see BUG-084.

[Unit]
Description=Luminos: capped memory budget for DrKonqi backtrace jobs (BUG-084)
Documentation=file:///home/shawn/luminos-os/docs/BUGS.md
Before=slices.target

[Slice]
MemoryAccounting=yes
MemoryMax=2G
MemorySwapMax=0
